| name=Ajuda Botanical Gardens | alt=Jardim Botânico da Ajuda | url=http://www.isa.ulisboa.pt/jba/apresentacao | email=botanicoajuda@isa.ulisboa.pt
| address=Calçada da Ajuda | lat=38.706208 | long=-9.200807 | directions=Tram stop {{station|Calçada da Ajuda (GNR)|18e}}
| phone=+351 21 362 2503 | tollfree= | fax=
| hours=Daily 09:00-20:00 (summer), 09:00-18:00 (winter) | price=€2
| image=Visão geral do Jardim Botânico da Ajuda.jpg | wikidata=Q5394216
| content=The botanical garden of Ajuda is one of the oldest gardens in Europe and is considered the first in Portugal. After the earthquake that occurred in 1755, the homeless Portuguese royal family decided to build a new royal residence at Ajuda but also gardens around it. This 10-acre garden was laid out in from 1858-1873.
}}
